  "idea": "A two-storey family house in northern Vietnamese timber, brick and terracotta, kept wholly inside the 13.5 × 19.7 m road-side ONT band. The entrance hall (Huyền Quan) is on the road. Living space runs north towards the garden. A 2.5 × 4 m east light court brings daylight and air into the middle of the deep plan. A 1.5 m service passage on the west side serves the wet kitchen and laundry without crossing the living rooms. Upstairs, three bedrooms, an altar room and a family lounge open onto a 2.2 m shaded balcony that looks over the existing garden land towards the river. Nothing is built on the DNN land.",
